# Kroxa escaped with the escape Underworld Breach gives it stays (CR 702.138b: a spell "escaped" if it was cast from a
# graveyard with an escape ability, its own or a granted one; the rulings sacrifice it only "if it was cast using any
# permission other than an escape ability"). Cast from hand on turn 1 (Mox Jet's {B}, Mox Ruby's {R}): Bot2 discards an
# Island, loses 3 (17), and Kroxa is sacrificed. On turn 3 Breach resolves (Mountain and Mox Ruby), three Lotus Petals go
# to the graveyard for {B}{R}{R}, and Kroxa, with only three other cards beside it, can't use its own escape but escapes
# by Breach's for its mana cost {B}{R}, exiling the three Petals. It stays; Bot2 discards an Island and loses 3 (14).

